36659241}, {\"transcription\": \"38.1\", \"points\": [[1396, 911], [1479, 911], [1479, 949], [1396, 949]], \"score\": 0.9999446868896484}, {\"transcription\": \"3.3.1018\", \"points\": [[1683, 908], [1879, 896], [1882, 948], [1686, 960]], \"score\": 0.9525694251060486}, {\"transcription\": \"Transformer (big)\", \"points\": [[561, 956], [873, 956], [873, 1000], [561, 1000]], \"score\": 0.9774637818336487}, {\"transcription\": \"28.4\", \"points\": [[1223, 956], [1310, 956], [1310, 997], [1223, 997]], \"score\": 0.9999369382858276}, {\"transcription\": \"41.8\", \"points\": [[1396, 956], [1479, 956], [1479, 997], [1396, 997]], \"score\": 0.9846281409263611}, {\"transcription\": \"2.3.1019\", \"points\": [[1697, 956], [1866, 948], [1868, 993], [1699, 1001]], \"score\": 0.9123871326446533}, {\"transcription\": \"Residual Dropout  We apply dropout [33] to the output of each sub-layer, before it is added to the\", \"points\": [[443, 1134], [2103, 1134], [2103, 1182], [443, 1182]], \"score\": 0.9800925254821777}, {\"transcription\": \"sub-layer input and normalized. In addition, we apply dropout to the sums of the embeddings and the\", \"points\": [[447, 1186], [2100, 1186], [2100, 1220], [447, 1220]], \"score\": 0.9882317781448364}, {\"transcription\": \" positional encodings in both the encoder and decoder stacks. For the base model, we use a rate of\", \"points\": [[440, 1227], [2106, 1224], [2107, 1268], [440, 1272]], \"score\": 0.9940704703330994}, {\"transcription\": \"Pdrop = 0.1.\", \"points\": [[443, 1272], [669, 1272], [669, 1320], [443, 1320]], \"score\": 0.941826581954956}, {\"transcription\": \"Label SmoothingDuring training, we employed label smoothing of value els = 0.1 [36]. This\", \"points\": [[440, 1372], [2100, 1375], [2100, 1423], [440, 1420]], \"score\": 0.9782333970069885}, {\"transcription\": \"hurts perplexity, as the model learns to be more unsure, but improves accuracy and BLEU score.\", \"points\": [[443, 1423], [2051, 1423], [2051, 1468], [443, 1468]], \"score\": 0.9937576055526733}, {\"transcription\": \"6Results\", \"points\": [[438, 1536], [687, 1544], [685, 1592], [436, 1584]], \"score\": 0.981620728969574}, {\"transcription\": \"6.1Machine Translation\", \"points\": [[443, 1650], [918, 1650], [918, 1695], [443, 1695]], \"score\": 0.9353169798851013}, {\"transcription\": \"On the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, the big transformer model (Transformer (big)\", \"points\": [[443, 1739], [2107, 1739], [2107, 1784], [443, 1784]], \"score\": 0.974907398223877}, {\"transcription\": \"in Table 2) outperforms the best previously reported models (including ensembles) by more than 2.0\", \"points\": [[443, 1784], [2107, 1784], [2107, 1829], [443, 1829]], \"score\": 0.9890804886817932}, {\"transcription\": \"BLEU, establishing a new state-of-the-art BLEU score of 28.4. The configuration of this model is\", \"points\": [[443, 1829], [2103, 1829], [2103, 1873], [443, 1873]], \"score\": 0.989074170589447}, {\"transcription\": \"listed in the bottom line of Table 3. Training took 3.5 days on 8 P100 GPUs. Even our base model\", \"points\": [[443, 1873], [2107, 1873], [2107, 1922], [443, 1922]], \"score\": 0.9830204844474792}, {\"transcription\": \"surpasses all previously published models and ensembles, at a fraction of the training cost of any of\", \"points\": [[443, 1922], [2107, 1922], [2107, 1966], [443, 1966]], \"score\": 0.9841927886009216}, {\"transcription\": \"the competitivemodels.\", \"points\": [[441, 1959], [853, 1967], [852, 2015], [440, 2007]], \"score\": 0.9923427104949951}, {\"transcription\": \" On the WMT 2014 English-to-French translation task, our big model achieves a BLEU score of 41.0,\", \"points\": [[440, 2028], [2107, 2032], [2106, 2080], [440, 2076]], \"score\": 0.9773122072219849}, {\"transcription\": \"outperforming all of the previously published single models, at less than 1/4 the training cost of the\", \"points\": [[443, 2076], [2103, 2076], [2103, 2124], [443, 2124]], \"score\": 0.9974532723426819}, {\"transcription\": \"previous state-of-the-art model. The Transformer (big) model trained for English-to-French used\", \"points\": [[447, 2124], [2100, 2124], [2100, 2173], [447, 2173]], \"score\": 0.9818764925003052}, {\"transcription\": \"dropout rate Pdrop = 0.1, instead of 0.3.\", \"points\": [[443, 2169], [1129, 2169], [1129, 2217], [443, 2217]], \"score\": 0.9590968489646912}, {\"transcription\": \"For the base models, we used a single model obtained by averaging the last 5 checkpoints, which\", \"points\": [[440, 2231], [2103, 2234], [2103, 2283], [440, 2279]], \"score\": 0.9885427355766296}, {\"transcription\": \"were written at 10-minute intervals. For the big models, we averaged the last 20 checkpoints. We\", \"points\": [[440, 2282], [2100, 2282], [2100, 2327], [440, 2327]], \"score\": 0.985663890838623}, {\"transcription\": \"used beam search with a beam size of 4 and length penalty α = 0.6 [38]. These hyperparameters\", \"points\": [[443, 2331], [2103, 2331], [2103, 2375], [443, 2375]], \"score\": 0.9950919151306152}, {\"transcription\": \"were chosen after experimentation on the development set. We set the maximum output length during\", \"points\": [[443, 2375], [2103, 2375], [2103, 2423], [443, 2423]], \"score\": 0.9912082552909851}, {\"transcription\": \" inference to input length + 50, but terminate early when possible [38].\", \"points\": [[440, 2420], [1621, 2417], [1622, 2465], [440, 2468]], \"score\": 0.990337610244751}, {\"transcription\": \"Table 2 summarizes our results and compares our translation quality and training costs to other model\", \"points\": [[447, 2489], [2103, 2489], [2103, 2533], [447, 2533]], \"score\": 0.9930775165557861}, {\"transcription\": \"architectures from the literature. We estimate the number of floating point operations used to train a\", \"points\": [[443, 2533], [2107, 2533], [2107, 2582], [443, 2582]], \"score\": 0.9718625545501709}, {\"transcription\": \"model by multiplying the training time, the number of GPUs used, and an estimate of the sustained\", \"points\": [[443, 2582], [2103, 2582], [2103, 2626], [443, 2626]], \"score\": 0.9879746437072754}, {\"transcription\": \"single-precision floating-point capacity of each GPU 5.\", \"points\": [[440, 2616], [1376, 2619], [1375, 2678], [440, 2674]], \"score\": 0.9672435522079468}, {\"transcription\": \"6.2Model Variations\", \"points\": [[443, 2736], [859, 2736], [859, 2781], [443, 2781]], \"score\": 0.9746220111846924}, {\"transcription\": \"To evaluate the importance of different components of the Transformer, we varied our base model\", \"points\": [[443, 2822], [2103, 2822], [2103, 2867], [443, 2867]], \"score\": 0.9939311742782593}, {\"transcription\": \"in different ways, measuring the change in performance on English-to-German translation on the\", \"points\": [[443, 2870], [2103, 2870], [2103, 2915], [443, 2915]], \"score\": 0.9973913431167603}, {\"transcription\": \" 5We used values of 2.8, 3.7, 6.0 and 9.5 TFLOPS for K80, K40, M40 and P100, respectively.\", \"points\": [[492, 2960], [1888, 2963], [1888, 3011], [492, 3008]], \"score\": 0.9893102645874023}]\n"
